# An OpenTheory article (format version 6, https://www.gilith.com/opentheory/article.html)
# in Gezi's encoding of a trace: the type term is the
# nullary type operator LambdaJit.term, and LambdaJit.choice : term -> term -> term. The
# article imports the commutativity of the choice, choice x y = choice y x, as an axiom with no hypotheses, instantiates it by subst
# with x := choice x y, and exports the instance with thm:
#   |- choice (choice x y) y = choice y (choice x y)
# The reader accepts it. A comment line starts with #; every other line is one command of
# the stack machine. The last use of every dictionary key is a remove, so the dictionary
# ends empty, as does the stack.
